      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Raymond Potterton are delighted to present this impressive five bedroom detached residence, superbly positioned on approximately 5.2 acres in the Hill of Ward, just outside Athboy. Set amid beautifully mature grounds, the property enjoys an exceptional degree of privacy and seclusion, enhanced by established trees, extensive planting and mature gardens.\n\nOriginally constructed circa 1972, the residence has been carefully and architecturally upgraded, modernised and extended over the years, creating a spacious and beautifully appointed family home combining character, quality and an abundance of natural light. The accommodation is particularly generous, with high ceilings throughout the principal living areas and a wonderful open plan kitchen and living space featuring a vaulted ceiling, bespoke\nCreative Wood kitchen with granite worktops and centre island, together with a bright sunroom opening directly onto the rear patio.\n\nThe property offers excellent bedroom accommodation with five bedrooms, including an impressive triple-aspect master suite with dressing room and ensuite, while several of the additional bedrooms benefit from ensuite or adjoining bathroom facilities.\n\nExternally, the property is approached through automated wrought iron gates and feature stone walls, opening onto an attractive tree lined driveway. The mature grounds are a particular feature, with extensive planting, beautifully maintained lawns and a superb front garden ideally suited as a private putting green. To the rear is a patio area creating an excellent setting for outdoor entertaining. There is an original foundation for an outdoor swimming pool\nwhich with some upgrading could be brought back into use.\n\nBeyond the residence is a substantial detached garage, large agricultural shed, concrete yard and two stables, benefiting from separate vehicular access.\n\nThe remaining lands are positioned to the rear in a good quality block, making the property particularly suitable for those with equestrian, hobby farming, business or recreational interests.\n\nOffering privacy, substantial accommodation and excellent ancillary facilities on an impressive mature holding, Hill of Ward represents a rare opportunity to acquire a distinctive family home in a highly regarded location close to Athboy.\n\nHill of Ward enjoys an attractive countryside setting within easy reach of Athboy, a thriving and well established town offering an excellent range of everyday amenities.\n\nAthboy provides supermarkets, shops, medical centre, cafés, restaurants, pharmacies and community facilities, together with both primary and secondary education at O'Growney National School and Athboy Community School. The town also has a strong sporting tradition with GAA, soccer, rugby and athletics clubs, along with a range of recreational and community amenities.\n\nThe property is also conveniently positioned for access to Trim, Navan and Kells, while the M3 motorway is approximately 15 minutes from Athboy, providing excellent connectivity towards Dublin and the wider motorway network. Regular bus services also connect Athboy with Dublin and surrounding towns, making the location an excellent balance between peaceful country living and accessibility.\n\nACCOMMODATION\n\nEntrance Porch - 2.53 x 2.05\nWith hardwood front door with large glass panels to the side, tiled flooring and feature panelling, double doors with large glass panes to Entrance Hall.\n\nEntrance Hall - 5.12 x 1.90\nWith wooden flooring, coving and recessed lights.\n\nLounge - 5.99 x 4.85\nWith carpet, feature ceiling, marble fireplace and solid fuel cassette stove insert and double doors with large glass panels to Dining.\n\nDining - 5.96 x 3.39\nDual aspect room with carpet and door to the Kitchen.\n\nKitchen - 7.57 x 5.29\nOpen plan space, kitchen with vaulted ceiling, bespoke built in wall and floor units with centre island, all with granite wortops, oven, hob, extractor fan and integrated dishwasher. Open plan to Living with feature ceiling, recessed lights, red brick fireplace with wooden mantle, panelling and Double doors to Sunroom.\n\nSunroom - 4.46 x 4.22\nWith wooden flooring and patio door to the rear patio.\n\nUtility / Pantry\nWith tiled flooring, washing machine, tumble dryer, fridge freezer and built in wall and floor units.\n\nBack Hall - 2.45 x 1.01\nWith tiled flooring and door to the rear.\n\nW.C. - 2.245 x 0.92\nTiled flooring, panelled walls, w.c. and w.h.b.\n\nBoot Room\nWith tiled flooring, Belfast sink and built in shelving.\n\nInner Hall - 10.54 x 1.24\nWith tiled flooring, hotpress, stira to the attic and vaulted ceiling provide natural light.\n\nMaster Suite - 5.50 x 4.12\nBeautiful triple aspect room with wooden flooring, tiled border open plan to dressing room with custom made built in wardrobe and built in storage providing the divide in this open plan Master Suite.\n\nEnsuite - 3.28 x 1.50\nFully tiled with w.h.b. with built in vanity and storage unit, walk in shower and heated towel rail, wall mounted mirrors and glass shelving.\n\nSeparate w.c. 1.36 x 1.30\nwith tiled floor, partially tiled wall, w.c. with tiled flooring and wall mounted w.h.b.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.76 x 3.29\nWith wooden flooring. \n\nWalk in Wardrobe 3.58 x 2.44\nWith wooden flooring and custom made built in wardrobes with folding doors.\n\nEnsuite - 3.76 x 3.29\nWith tiled flooring, partially tiled wall, w.c., w.h.b. shower and heated towel rail.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.48 x 3.30\nWith wooden flooring and built in open shelving.\n\nEnsuite - 1.77 x 1.63\nFully tiled with w.c., wall mounted w.h.b. shower, heated towel rail and valulted ceiling with glass insert.\n\nBedroom 4 - 4.68 x 3.43\nWith wooden flooring, wall to ceiling sliderobes with mirrored doors. Door to Bathroom.\n\nBathroom- 3.33 x1.93\nFully tiled with w.c., wall mounted w.h.b., shower, bath and heated towel rail with two doors to the hall and serving \nBedroom 4.\n\nStudy / Bedroom 5\nWith dual windows semi solid wooden flooring built in corner storage / wardrobes.\n\nGarage - 9.07 x 6.2\nWith garage door and electricity\n\nShed - 18.6 x 15.3\nPart block and steel framed shed with double sliding doors.\n\nTwo Stables\nBlock built with wooden doors.\n\nFEATURES\n\n•Impressive five-bedroom detached family residence\n•Set on approximately 5.2 acres of mature private grounds and quality lands\n•Residence carefully upgraded, modernised and architecturally extended\n•Superb bespoke Creative Wood kitchen with granite worktops and centre island\n•Private tree-lined driveway with automated wrought-iron entrance gates\n•Beautifully maintained mature gardens, lawns and extensive planting\n•Original foundations for an outdoor swimming pool\n•Adjoining patio area\n•Large detached garage\n•Excellent setting close to Athboy, Trim, Navan, Kells and the M3 motorway\n\nOUTSIDE\n\n•Substantial yard with large agricultural shed\n•Quality block of lands to the rear\n•Gated access to the lands\n•Two stables and separate vehicular access to the yard and lands\n\nSERVICES\n\n•Well\n•Rainwater system\n•Mains sewerage\n•Solar panels\n•Oil fired central heating\n\nDIRECTIONS\n\nEIRCODE: C15 VY63"
      },
